=== Test 1: shm_echo client demo ===
=========================================
Running: shm_echo_client
=========================================
╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
║    Shared Memory Echo Client - Direct Transport Demo    ║
╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

NOTE: This example demonstrates the shared memory transport
working at the transport layer. Standard gRPC examples require
additional integration work to use grpc.NewClient()/NewServer().

The transport layer is fully functional with:
  ✓ Futex-based synchronization
  ✓ Zero-copy shared memory ring buffers
  ✓ Bidirectional streaming without deadlocks
  ✓ HTTP/2-style frame protocol

What's missing for standard gRPC examples:
  ✗ Integration with grpc.NewClient()
  ✗ Integration with grpc.NewServer()
  ✗ Custom resolver for shm:// URLs
  ✗ Transport interface bridge layer

For working demos, see the test files:
  - internal/transport/shm/client_unary_test.go
  - internal/transport/shm/cancel_unary_test.go
  - internal/transport/shm/streaming_test.go

Run tests with:
  go test -v ./internal/transport/shm -run TestUnary


✅ shm_echo_client: SUCCESS


